# Entry point and daemon assembly

- `cmd/golem-deploy` parses subcommands with stdlib `flag` (`serve`, `admin create|reset-password`, `version`; no arguments prints usage and exits 2). Flags have `GOLEM_DEPLOY_*` environment fallbacks; there is no config file. Never prompt on stdin during `serve`.
- `internal/daemon.Run` is the composition root: data directory, keys, store, `Reconcile`, git runner (with startup sweeps of git scratch files and orphaned checkouts; nil when git is missing), job runner, `httpapi.Server`. On context cancellation HTTP shutdown and job cancellation run together and the store closes last. It refuses plaintext HTTP on non-loopback addresses before touching disk (`httpapi.CheckListen`).
- `internal/datadir` owns the data directory layout (0700 directories, 0600 key files; key files readable by group or others are refused on Unix). All runtime paths come from `datadir.Layout`; nothing is written relative to the working directory.
- `internal/daemon/admin.go` backs the `admin` CLI and works while the daemon runs (SQLite WAL).
- `frontend/embed.go` embeds `frontend/dist` (`all:dist`); without `index.html` it serves a plain-text 503 notice. Only paths outside `/api/` reach it.
- Changes to flags, environment variables or the data directory layout must update `README.md`.
- Verify with `go test ./cmd/... ./internal/daemon/... ./internal/datadir/... ./frontend/...`.
